{"id": "EUVD-2026-76521", "enisaUuid": "7b7d36a3-5272-3329-b9f3-cac53b7d6110", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\necryptfs: hold msg ctx list lock when cleaning daemon queue\n\necryptfs_exorcise_daemon() drops queued messages from a dying daemon\nwithout holding ecryptfs_msg_ctx_lists_mux, but\necryptfs_msg_ctx_alloc_to_free() requires that lock.\n\nTake the list lock while moving the queued contexts back to the free\nlist to avoid racing with other global msg ctx list users.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:41", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64d8998e36cfd2bb7114f3af0aa51c5a559a39b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d50b8aea11ad9594c8704a4c647e11311ab7b19", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/956541efd125a10442f9514668bc5c852702c93b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec1627bcb5b51ddd46b1ef27a9d5a9834abb0a6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7e48afafe7abc275f7b6916613bb18b821e7d94a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d9636ecba34bd553ecf19049f7705505aea62fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c02acbe0a2692ca9991c51e62bbe6d6b59dac31", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/779972513c2fa8c7938e54976f686091dafff22f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89609", "GHSA-c77f-5fp9-7h2f"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08bdadb9-3309-30bb-8421-e51ec15a9cbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f66e883eb6186bc43a79581b67aff7d1a69d0ff1 <779972513c2fa8c7938e54976f686091dafff22f"}, {"id": "225522ed-8d3a-3b1b-b30d-11fcf0a66065", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "3bf058b8-2910-38e7-bc06-71972b856490", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "3f431be6-1d07-3b11-aabf-101e3ca897